<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-17T22:08:51+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:08:51 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[30 lions and tigers leave notorious Argentine zoo; head to new sanctuaries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133295851.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Thirty lions and tigers from Argentina’s shuttered Lujan Zoo have begun a major relocation to wildlife sanctuaries in South Africa and the US. Led by Four Paws, the rescue involves moving 30 big cats that spent years in cramped cages and suffered health problems. The animals will now travel to Lionsrock in South Africa and The Wild Animal Sanctuary in Colorado.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-lions-and-tigers-spent-years-in-cramped-concrete-cages-at-a-notorious-argentine-zoo-they-are-now-beginning-a-journey-to-sanctuaries-where-they-can-finally-roam-freely/articleshow/133295851.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-lions-and-tigers-spent-years-in-cramped-concrete-cages-at-a-notorious-argentine-zoo-they-are-now-beginning-a-journey-to-sanctuaries-where-they-can-finally-roam-freely/articleshow/133295851.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T22:06:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133298371,imgsize-119602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Only nine such butterflies were found in US in 2022; 3 years later, over 1,300 were released]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133273631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers in Michigan have helped bring the Poweshiek skipperling butterfly back from the brink of extinction after its US wild population fell to just nine in 2022. Through captive breeding, habitat restoration and carefully planned releases, more than 1,300 butterflies were released in 2025. The recovery effort has now expanded to other endangered butterflies, while restored prairie habitats are helping support wider ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/only-nine-of-these-butterflies-were-found-across-the-us-in-2022-three-years-later-researchers-released-more-than-1300-to-rebuild-the-species/articleshow/133273631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/only-nine-of-these-butterflies-were-found-across-the-us-in-2022-three-years-later-researchers-released-more-than-1300-to-rebuild-the-species/articleshow/133273631.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T22:06:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msi