 Experiments showed Camponotus castaneus ants consumed the most waste, proving effective.  Her prototype achieved an impressive eighty-three percent efficiency in initial tests.  This research offers a novel biological approach to managing discarded food materials.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ananya-nagendra-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-built-an-ant-based-digester-for-landfill-food-waste-tests-found-her-prototype-was-about-83-efficient/articleshow/133298125.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-ananya-nagendra-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-built-an-ant-based-digester-for-landfill-food-waste-tests-found-her-prototype-was-about-83-efficient/articleshow/133298125.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:43:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133298195,imgsize-1438492.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kay Cottee sailed solo around the world in 189 days, making history]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133297589.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1987-australian-sailor-kay-cottee-left-sydney-alone-in-a-37-foot-yacht-after-building-a-boat-charter-business-to-fund-her-dream-189-days-later-she-became-the-first-woman-to-sail-solo-nonstop-and-unassisted-around-the-world/articleshow/133297589.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1987-australian-sailor-kay-cottee-left-sydney-alone-in-a-37-foot-yacht-after-building-a-boat-charter-business-to-fund-her-dream-189-days-later-she-became-the-first-woman-to-sail-solo-nonstop-and-unassisted-around-the-world/articleshow/133297589.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:3