ription><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-usain-bolt-i-stopped-worrying-about-the-start-the-end-is-a-lesson-on-letting-go-of-a-shaky-beginning-and-focusing-on-the-finish/articleshow/133296524.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-usain-bolt-i-stopped-worrying-about-the-start-the-end-is-a-lesson-on-letting-go-of-a-shaky-beginning-and-focusing-on-the-finish/articleshow/133296524.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:45:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133296758,imgsize-90117.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman donates $1 million to the teachers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133295133.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A generous donation of one million dollars was given to teachers in California. One hundred educators in the Ross Valley School District received substantial bonuses. This significant gift came from a local resident concerned about teacher compensation. The teachers expressed deep gratitude for this unexpected and life-changing financial support. The donor hopes her action will inspire others to support public education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/100-teachers-walked-into-a-meeting-expecting-an-ordinary-day-they-walked-out-with-over-9000-each-as-a-california-woman-offers-life-changing-bonuses-to-educators-struggling-with-low-salaries/articleshow/133295133.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/100-teachers-walked-into-a-meeting-expecting-an-ordinary-day-they-walked-out-with-over-9000-each-as-a-california-woman-offers-life-changing-bonuses-to-educators-struggling-with-low-salaries/articleshow/133295133.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T17:10:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133295712,imgsize-210115.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How 14-year-old Miles Wu is using origami to design stronger shelters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133295421.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking study, young scholar Miles Wu delves into the use of origami techniques for emergency shelters. He meticulously examined fifty-four variations of the Miura-ori pattern and discovered that some designs could withstand more than nine thousand times their own weight. This ancient art form uncovers new possibilities for portable disaster relief structures. Wu’s research underscores the importance of geometric principles in enhancing the efficiency of materials.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-miles-wu-the-14-year-old-new-york-student-using-origami-to-explore-stronger-foldable-emergency-shelters/articleshow/133295421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-miles-wu-the-14-year-old-new-york-student-using-origami-to-explore-stronger-foldable-emergency-shelters/articleshow/133295421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T18:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133295637,imgsize-1038504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Doja Cat’s response to a Twitch viewer asking about streaming quotas goes viral]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133293757.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Doja Cat recently explained her Twitch streaming motivations to fans. She clarified that she streams purely for enjoyment and personal satisfaction. The singer highlighted her elaborate room decor and outfits as proof of this. She stated that if quotas were her goal, she would appear in simple sweatpants. This approach shows her relaxed attitude towards the platform.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cats-response-to-a-twitch-viewer-asking-about-streaming-quotas-goes-viral/articleshow/133293757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/doja-cats-response-to-a-twitch-viewer-asking-about-streaming-quotas-goes-viral/articleshow/133293757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T15:59:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133293846,imgsize-672987.cms"/></item></channel></rss>